What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../power_cycle_seconds
Date:		November 2026
Contact:		Mark Featherston <mark@embeddedts.com>
Description:
		Writing a positive integer immediately powers off the system and
		restarts it after the requested number of seconds. This does not
		perform an orderly Linux shutdown or sync filesystems; userspace
		must do so before writing. The maximum accepted value is 42949672
		seconds for generation 1 controllers and 16777215 seconds for
		generation 0 controllers.
		Actual off time depends on the controller's low-power clock.

What: 		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../pushsw_wake_en
Date: 		November 2026
Contact: 	Mark Featherston <mark@embeddedts.com>
Description:
		Read or write 1 to enable the active-low push switch to wake the
		system during a timed power cycle, or 0 to disable it. The default
		is 1. This file is present only on boards whose supervisor firmware
		supports this setting. It affects the next reset or timed power cycle.
